Tokenizer source and vocabulary notices
=======================================

These retained third-party files have component-specific terms. The repository
root license does not replace those terms. Keep this notice, ../../data/README.md,
the applicable ../../data/LICENSE.* files and file-specific .NOTICE sidecars with
copies of the corresponding cached files and their transformed tables.

cl100k_base.tiktoken, o200k_base.tiktoken:
  OpenAI tiktoken; Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI, Shantanu Jain.
  ../../data/LICENSE.openai-tiktoken (MIT).

qwen3.8.tokenizer.json:
  Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B; Copyright 2026 Alibaba Cloud.
  ../../data/LICENSE.qwen3.8 (Apache-2.0), including its attribution appendix.
  This cache is modified; see qwen3.8.tokenizer.json.NOTICE.

kimi.tiktoken.model, tokenization_kimi.py:
  The OMP cache identifies Kimi K3, despite the kimi_k2 packed output name.
  Copyright (c) 2026 Moonshot AI; ../../data/LICENSE.kimi-k3.
  Both files exactly match K3 snapshot f831ab66814297da540d832a5235f8e904f29d06.
  The vocabulary also matches Moonshot's Kimi-VL-A3B-Instruct release; its
  separate MIT notice is retained in ../../data/LICENSE.kimi-vl.
  The Python file's existing Xenova citation is preserved. Separate permission
  for its exact byte-mapping expression was determined unnecessary by the narrow
  U.S. copyright assessment in ../../data/README.md; no notebook license is asserted.

deepseek-v3.tokenizer.json, deepseek-v4.tokenizer.json:
  DeepSeek; Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek.
  ../../data/LICENSE.deepseek reproduces the publisher's MIT license wording.
  V4 matches DeepSeek-V4-Pro JSON in full, except formatting/object-key order.
  V3 is byte-identical to the publisher's MIT-licensed DeepSeek-V3-0324 snapshot.
  The original V3 model agreement is retained as historical context only in
  ../../data/LICENSE.deepseek-v3-model. See README for exact matching pins.

glm-5.tokenizer.json:
  Full JSON content matches pinned zai-org/GLM-5 (Z.ai), except formatting/
  object-key order. ../../data/LICENSE.glm5 retains the publisher's verbatim
  license: mit declaration and standard MIT permission/warranty terms.
  The publisher snapshot supplied no copyright line; no holder/year is invented.

ctok_v3.bin, ctok_v4_7.bin:
  Generated ctok vocabulary data; preserve ../../data/LICENSE.ctok unchanged.

This is a source provenance/notice record, not a publication approval. Exact
evidence, transformations and remaining prerequisites are in ../../data/README.md.
